#: background.md:1
msgid "[&larr; Home](NAVIGATION.md)"
msgstr "[&larr; ホーム](NAVIGATION.md)"

#: background.md:3
msgid "Background of `maze`"
msgstr "`maze` の背景"

#: background.md:5
msgid ""
"In molecular dynamics, it has been challenging to search for reaction "
"pathways that describe rare events in complex systems. Incorrectly computed "
"reaction pathways can lead to issues with calculating free energies and "
"kinetic rates."
msgstr ""
"MD では、複雑な系の Rare Events を記述する Reaction Pathways の探索が難しい課題となってきた。Reaction "
"Pathways を誤って求めると、自由エネルギーや Kinetic Rates の計算に問題が生じうる。"

#: background.md:7
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will explore an enhanced sampling technique to identify"
" ligand unbinding pathways from proteins. This will involve optimizing a "
"loss function that characterizes ligand-protein interactions. Our analysis "
"will focus on the T4 lysozyme L99A mutant (T4L) with benzene in its binding "
"pocket. This mutant is commonly utilized as a model system for studying how "
"ligands bind to proteins."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは、タンパク質からの Ligand Unbinding Pathways を特定する Enhanced Sampling "
"手法を扱う。Ligand-Protein Interactions を特徴付ける Loss Function を最適化する。対象は、Binding "
"Pocket に Benzene を含む T4 Lysozyme L99A Mutant（T4L）である。この Mutant は、Ligands "
"とタンパク質の結合を調べるモデル系として広く用いられる。"

#: background.md:9
msgid "Loss Function"
msgstr "Loss Function"

#: background.md:10
msgid ""
"Because fluctuations in binding pockets are important for dissociation, we "
"will employ a loss function that scores how deeply buried a ligand is within"
" the protein matrix. This loss function should have a maximum within the "
"protein and decrease to zero as the ligand dissociates to solvent."
msgstr ""
"Binding Pockets のゆらぎは Dissociation に重要なので、Ligand が Protein Matrix "
"にどれだけ深く埋もれているかを評価する Loss Function を用いる。この関数は、タンパク質の内部で最大となり、Ligand が溶媒へ "
"Dissociation するにつれて0に近づくものとする。"

#: background.md:12
msgid ""
"For simplicity, we will use a very simple model for ligand-protein "
"interactions:"
msgstr "簡単のため、Ligand-Protein Interactions に非常に単純なモデルを用いる。"

#: background.md:18
msgid ""
"where the sum goes over ligand-protein atom pairs in the local neighborhood "
"of the ligand and $r_0$ is a cutoff. The new version of `maze` can use any "
"loss function implemented in PLUMED as a [switching "
"function](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/switchingfunction.html)."
msgstr ""
"和は、Ligand の局所近傍の Ligand-Protein 原子対について取る。$r_0$ は Cutoff である。新しい `maze` "
"では、PLUMED の [Switching Function](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/switchingfunction.html) として実装された任意の関数を Loss Function に使える。"

#: background.md:20
msgid "Minimization"
msgstr "Minimization"

#: background.md:21
msgid ""
"We will minimize the loss function using simulated annealing. In this "
"method, we check if a randomly chosen neighboring position of the ligand "
"corresponds to a decrease in the loss function. The probability of accepting"
" a randomly generated neighbor is given by:"
msgstr ""
"Simulated Annealing で Loss Function を最小化する。Ligand の近傍から位置をランダムに選び、Loss "
"Function が小さくなるかを調べる。生成した近傍位置を受理する確率は、次のようになる。"

#: background.md:27
msgid ""
"where $\\Delta L$ is the difference between the current loss function and "
"the loss function of the neighbor, and $\\beta$ is a tempering parameter "
"(see [Input](input.md))."
msgstr ""
"$\\Delta L$ は現在位置と近傍位置での Loss Function の差、$\\beta$ は Tempering Parameter "
"である。[入力](input.md)を参照してほしい。"

#: background.md:29
msgid "Adaptive Biasing"
msgstr "Adaptive Biasing"

#: background.md:30
msgid ""
"After minimization converges and identifies the optimal unbinding direction "
"$w_k$ is determined, the current position of the ligand $x$ is biased toward"
" $w_k$. This is accomplished by applying an adaptive harmonic potential:"
msgstr ""
"Minimization が収束して最適な Unbinding Direction $w_k$ が決まったら、Ligand の現在位置 $x$ から "
"$w_k$ に向けて Bias を加える。Adaptive Harmonic Potential を用いて実現する。"

#: background.md:36
msgid ""
"where $w_k$ is the optimal solution at step $k$, $v$ is the biasing rate, "
"$h$ is the scale constant, and $\\Delta t$ is the MD time between subsequent"
" loss function minimizations. A detailed explanation can be found in "
"[[1]](#1)."
msgstr ""
"$w_k$ はステップ $k$ での最適解、$v$ は Biasing Rate、$h$ は Scale Constant、$\\Delta t$ "
"は連続する Loss Function の最小化の間の MD 時間である。詳しい説明は [[1]](#1) にある。"

#: background.md:40
msgid ""
"*Figure* Unbinding is initiated from the bound state (X-ray binding site) of"
" the T4L-benzene complex and ends once the ligand reaches the solvent. (a) "
"The cross-section through the X-ray structure of T4L shows no apparent "
"tunnels for benzene to leave the protein, which means that the protein must "
"undergo structural changes to open possible exits. (b) A reaction pathway "
"characterizing the unbinding along the exit tunnel is identified locally "
"during MD simulations. (c) To determine the (k+1)-th intermediate, the "
"conformations of benzene are sampled in the neighborhood of the k-th "
"intermediate. Then, the optimal biasing direction is calculated from the "
"sampled ligand conformations by selecting the ligand conformation with the "
"lowest loss function value."
msgstr ""
"*図* Unbinding は、T4L-Benzene Complex の Bound State（X-ray Binding "
"Site）から始まり、Ligand が溶媒に達すると終わる。(a) T4L の X-ray Structure の断面には、Benzene "
"がタンパク質から脱出する明確な Tunnel がない。このため、出口を開くにはタンパク質の構造変化が必要である。(b) MD 中に、出口の Tunnel"
" に沿う Unbinding を特徴付ける Reaction Pathway を局所的に特定する。(c) (k+1) 番目の Intermediate "
"を決めるため、k 番目の Intermediate の近傍で Benzene の Conformations を Sampling する。最小の "
"Loss Function を持つ Conformation を選び、最適な Biasing Direction を求める。"

